.TH sway-things-hook 1 "" "Sway Things 0.4.0" "Sway Things Manual"
.SH NAME
sway\-things\-hook \- Run a hook; the generated sway config runs these
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsway\-things hook\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a hook; the generated sway config runs these
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Controls when to use color
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-gsettings(1)
Copy the stored settings that GTK apps read from GSettings (cursor theme and size) to GSettings; run at login and at each reload of sway
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-displays(1)
Switch a display on if none is on (and have kanshi apply its profile again, if it runs): run at every start and reload of sway while Sway Things stores anything for a display, so it never leaves you without one
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-workspaces(1)
Put the workspaces on the displays connected now as the Workspaces page says: run at every start and reload of sway while a rule places them, and by kanshi when it applied a profile
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-mirror(1)
Show displays on others as remembered for the displays connected now (wl\-mirror), and end the mirrors of other combinations: run by kanshi when it applied a profile, and from a key binding of yours to bring back a picture that went
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-new\-display(1)
Ask once whether a display plugged in to a combination set up on the Displays page shows the same picture or extends the desktop, and remember the answer: run by kanshi when one display more than such a combination is connected
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-wallpaper(1)
Show the next picture of each wallpaper collection whose time has come, and start the timers of those that change daily or after an interval: run when sway starts while a display shows a collection
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-clipboard(1)
Start the watcher of the clipboard history (wl\-paste \-\-watch cliphist store) if the Screenshots & Clipboard page has the history on, and end it if not: run at every start and reload of sway while it is on
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-launch(1)
Start an installed app by its desktop file ID, as its desktop entry says (in a terminal if it asks for one): the autostart entries of Sway Things that are apps run this
.TP
sway\-things\-hook\-autostart(1)
Hand the session\*(Aqs variables to the systemd user session and start the XDG autostart entries through it (xdg\-desktop\-autostart.target): run at login while Sway Things starts them with systemd
